{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense","id":1026232,"title":"Lupus *With* Resources? How The Heck Does THAT Make Sense?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-03T17:23:12-08:00","id":1026232,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Lupus *With* Resources? How The Heck Does THAT Make Sense?","content":"Dear White Wolf.<br /> <br /> Here is an issue that I found contradictory ever since the First/Second Edition.<br /> Okay, it makes *sense* that a Lupus Garou cannot *Start* with Human Skills (Crafts, Drive, Ettique, Firearms, Larceny, Academics, Computer, Law, Science, Technology) without spending *Freebie* points: It does represent your &quot;Life Experience Customization&quot; after leaving the life of a normal wolf, after all.<br /> <br /> But not ONCE in ALL the editions, has it been restricted for a Lupus Garou to buy The <b>Resources</b> Background with the Five Points of Background Available to ALL Characters. How the heck does that make sense?<br /> <br /> Sure, a Metis can (somehow) through the years he spent in the family basement learn how to read and more than certainly surf-the-internet and learn about Human Society and Skills, an can most certainly be written as &quot;My Inbred Cousin with Bad Teeth Called Cletus&quot; in the Family Will and thereby gain points in Resources.<br /> <br /> But how in the heck is a Fresh Out of the Forrest Lupus going to even get a job at the Local 7-11 and Otooleys to even get ONE Dot in Resources as he is?<br /> <br /> (Ted voice from Bill and Ted's Excellent Adventure) Like How Dude, How?<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:14:27-08:00","id":1026249,"title":"","content":"While I might state their is some responsibility for the sense of character concept to be laid at the feet of STs and players, there are a few edge cases where resources may make sense.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers, Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, and similar tribes for instance may very well have small trusts built up from tribal wealth that can simply be turned over to them upon being discovered. Generally this won't be super mega-bucks, but a few small annuities can greatly help young confused cubs.<br /> <br /> More deep woods characters might have a cache of natural resources, treasure, or similar saleable goods they can tap for the needed wealth, or start up capital.<br /> <br /> A lupus may lack human skills, but I bet one could pick up extortion and shake-downs pretty quick. If they have a regular area they hit, then that could equal resources. Blackmail and identity theft would require the right circumstances, but could be profitable.<br /> <br /> Eccentric wealthy people have been noted to both keep odd pets and leave fortunes of money to those pets, although I'd probably avoid going to the well too often on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:20:53-08:00","id":1026251,"title":"","content":"Yea, pretty much everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1136\" data-vbnamecard=\"1136\">Wolfgar</a> stated. If a Lupus player wants the Resources background, it should make sense. If their reason doesn't then feel free to say no. There are several reasons it can happen, though I've yet to encounter a Lupus player who wanted them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T22:47:55-08:00","id":1026341,"title":"","content":"Also, starting level characters are not &quot;fresh out of the woods,&quot; they've all received enough training and experience to gain Renown, Rank, and be initiated into a Tribe.<br /> <br /> This means a Lupus character has had the time to, say, learn enough to be able to establish a source of income. Frankly, the far bigger issue for a lupus is not learning anything (Lupus characters are just as intelligence and capable of learning as Metis and Homid characters) but that Lupus would have incredible trouble finding above the table legal employment because they weren't born human with the proper paperwork. Lupus don't come with birth certificates or other credentials.<br /> <br /> Even in real life, people that for whatever reasons are born without documentation can have their lives ruined by it as they become adults and try to get jobs and so on. Lupus (and really Metis as well) that want to blend in and have some cash are going to be extremely reliant on the Garou/Kinfolk around them for it; either through working off the books, or for having someone to get them sufficiently good fake documents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:29:34-08:00","id":1026501,"title":"","content":"Watching the History Channel has taught me that the Knights Templar and NAZI's buried untold amounts of pilfered gold in various places around the world. Clearly any Lupus with a lot of resources found some in their life experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:15:54-08:00","id":1026530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1026501#post1026501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching the History Channel has taught me that the Knights Templar and NAZI's buried untold amounts of pilfered gold in various places around the world. Clearly any Lupus with a lot of resources found some in their life experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooh, so THAT'S what the Storyteller's Handbooks across all the World of Darkness Games Across The Editions MEAN when they said &quot;Dots In Resources Can Writes Entire Plotlines: You don't need to do all the work, the Players' Backgrounds do half the work for you.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:24:01-08:00","id":1026536,"title":"","content":"I kind of want to make a Lupus Galliard/Ragabash treasure hunter now. What tribe would fit that concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:50:04-08:00","id":1026574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1026536#post1026536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of want to make a Lupus Galliard/Ragabash treasure hunter now. What tribe would fit that concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most could. The Tribes are built fairly open ended that way. If you are talking purely about human wealth/treasure, then maybe the Talons or Wendigo less so. Probably not the Stargazers with their anti-materialism philosophy. But otherwise, you can write a decent character concept like this with most of the Tribes. I think a Bone Gnawer treasure hunter would be fun, if only because Resources is/was a discouraged/barred background for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:16:14-08:00","id":1026588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1026574#post1026574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most could. The Tribes are built fairly open ended that way. If you are talking purely about human wealth/treasure, then maybe the Talons or Wendigo less so. Probably not the Stargazers with their anti-materialism philosophy. But otherwise, you can write a decent character concept like this with most of the Tribes. I think a Bone Gnawer treasure hunter would be fun, if only because Resources is/was a discouraged/barred background for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Bone Gnawer, but Silver Fang may be interesting too (searching for family history and all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:22:23-08:00","id":1026591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1026588#post1026588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking Bone Gnawer, but Silver Fang may be interesting too (searching for family history and all).</div> </div> </div> </div>Striders also work easily enough. Fianna and Get can both also do the family historical treasures. Uktena can, with a more mystical artifact take on the treasure hunting. Furies fall somewhere between the 2 for me. Shadow Lords could easily be looking to find treasure (theirs of anybody else's). And those are just off the top of my head. Individuals from the other Tribes could be written with similar reasons easily enough.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:27:51-08:00","id":1026595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1026591#post1026591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Striders also work easily enough. Fianna and Get can both also do the family historical treasures. Uktena can, with a more mystical artifact take on the treasure hunting. Furies fall somewhere between the 2 for me. Shadow Lords could easily be looking to find treasure (theirs of anybody else's). And those are just off the top of my head. Individuals from the other Tribes could be written with similar reasons easily enough.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There could be a whole pack of treasure hunters from various tribes. I imagine they break into museums, raid archaeological sites, go on umbra quests to reclaim lost fetishes and the like. *files idea away for future use*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:44:05-08:00","id":1026605,"title":"","content":"I can imagine an entire pack of Get of Fenris being supported by the income produced by the investments bought by their Human Kinfolk with Nazi gold after the war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:05:50-08:00","id":1026616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1026595#post1026595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There could be a whole pack of treasure hunters from various tribes. I imagine they break into museums, raid archaeological sites, go on umbra quests to reclaim lost fetishes and the like. *files idea away for future use*</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say that there should already be such a pack in canon. I know there is a Fury Caern that stockpiles fetishes/treasures. So I have to imagine that they would require having a journeying pack to actually go out and secure said items.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly a money/treasure hunting pack, but it's along those lines. I could see a pack with O'Mighty Dollar as a totem who went out and hunted down monetary wealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:59:08-08:00","id":1026788,"title":"","content":"one way Ive handled it, is for them to have a human kinfolk, or garou who see's them as family, and acts as a benefactor.<br /> <br /> <br /> a lot of garou probaly Derive their Resources from &quot;gifts&quot; from local kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:03:26-08:00","id":1026807,"title":"","content":"Relating to this subject. A lupus should be able to, without handholding, manage to keep the veil in the city at least somewhat. They are adult in the eyes of the Nation at Cliath, so expecting their pack to coddle them due to their breed is weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:11:06-08:00","id":1026809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1026807#post1026807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relating to this subject. A lupus should be able to, without handholding, manage to keep the veil in the city at least somewhat. They are adult in the eyes of the Nation at Cliath, so expecting their pack to coddle them due to their breed is weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can they not? By the time a Garou reaches rank 1, they should be passibly adept at using all of their forms. That means Homids should know the basics of running on 4 legs and Lupus can pass as humans, even if they seem a bit odd. I always thought that was a given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T20:43:09-08:00","id":1026839,"title":"","content":"red talons might still be totally inept, other tribes, will have at least the basics of pretending to be human down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T21:47:55-08:00","id":1026853,"title":"","content":"I imagine that most Lupus will know the basics of human behavior, even if they think that it is rather silly. They will not go out naked (though they may strip down when they get home, even if they do not change) and will not use the bathroom in public. They will probably be able to answer a phone and may even enjoy fast food. They may even take a liking to sex in the human form, as the human body is capable of having sex for hours while the wolf body is only capable of having sex for minutes (though they will probably wonder why humans do not have a bone in their penis).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T22:56:26-08:00","id":1026873,"title":"","content":"Two words: Blue Steel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:16:22-08:00","id":1026915,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing that Glass Walkers would be awfully popular among Urban Lupus who *don't* want to sleep in dumpsters all the time in forging fake ID's so they can ACTUALLY get that interview at the Local Pub. And no doubt more than a few Silver Fangs would owe the Walkers hefty favors from forging Birth Certificates for &quot;Embarrassments&quot; who can *finally* assume human form but need to climb the corporate ladder *quick* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In terms of Birth Certificates, Baby Photos can (rather morbidly, yes) be scavenged from the morgue, but what about the more-than-a little unique fingerprints and foot-prints that almost all modern babies in Westernized Hospitals press onto said-certificates?<br /> <br /> And back on the subject of cash:<br /> <br /> 1A) In terms of &quot;accurate roleplaying&quot;, would Lupus in general be more comfortable with a &quot;Cash Box&quot; (IE. Toolbox) of banknotes rather than an electronic bank account?<br /> <br /> 1B) For that matter, a &quot;modern setting&quot; (late 20th to 21st Century) World of Darkness Character of Any Game (minus Wraith for obvious reasons) NEEDS an Electronically Accessible Bank Account to have even Resources 1, yes?<br /> <br /> 2) One gets the feeling the Almighty Dollar Totem would not be very friendly or even ACCEPT packs that have Bone Gnawers, as they are the very antithesis of the American Dream he stands for.<br /> <br /> Back to Flute Practice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-05-2017, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T12:34:17-08:00","id":1027220,"title":"","content":"1A) It's hard to say how Lupus as a generality would feel about cash vs. banking. Cash would be easier to understand (heck, plenty of humans IRL don't really get how banking works) as a system (&quot;It's like bargaining with Spirits with Gnosis instead of doing quests for them. You give them enough and they will do what you ask if you asked right.&quot;), but if they're not really managing their money themselves they're not going to care how a kin does it for them as long as it seems to be working.<br /> <br /> 1B) Incorrect. While it is rare/difficult in modern times in developed societies, there are still cash only (and in some places barter primary) people around.<br /> <br /> 2) Not necessarily. O'Mighty tends to prefer high finance and banks, but being the big fish in a little pond that makes the money move is still something he likes. The Barksdale Crew from the Wire could easily be a Gnawer run organization with the pack following O'Mighty to ensure the cash flow for the kin that make up the leadership of the gang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:17:02-08:00","id":1027396,"title":"","content":"&quot;How did my character get resources 5? Well one day my Red Talon was out in the woods and he found the corpse of a guy hanging from a tree by a parachute and at his feet was a suitcase filled with $1 million in cash...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:26:56-08:00","id":1027400,"title":"","content":"I live in Louisville, Ky, and There are many people that work off the books. They get paid in cash and have no bank accounts. There are many rooming houses that charge about $75 a week for a room. There are also a lot of labor pool companies that hire day labor for all sorts of work ( warehouse, sports centers, restaurants, hotels, etc.). To cash their checks, they go to many convenience stores which will cash any check for about $3.00. A local store by where I live probably cashes around a thousand checks a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:33:09-08:00","id":1027404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1027396#post1027396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;How did my character get resources 5? Well one day my Red Talon was out in the woods and he found the corpse of a guy hanging from a tree by a parachute and at his feet was a suitcase filled with $1 million in cash...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoa! If that was a Drug-Lord's Money....<br /> <br /> &quot;Tonight at the Grindhouse Drive-In Double Feature! Werewolf Cokeheads VS Columbian UZI Pimps!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though more seriously:<br /> <br /> Would &quot;My Family's Territory is centered around an abandoned Gold-Mine Ghost Town&quot; be also a plausible explanation for Lupus Wealth? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would imagine though that wealthy though he may be, this Lupus is NOT going to be popular with the local &quot;Bird and Lizard Population.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-05-2017, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T21:45:59-08:00","id":1027445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1027404#post1027404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Whoa! If that was a Drug-Lord's Money....<br /> <br /> &quot;Tonight at the Grindhouse Drive-In Double Feature! Werewolf Cokeheads VS Columbian UZI Pimps!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though more seriously:<br /> <br /> Would &quot;My Family's Territory is centered around an abandoned Gold-Mine Ghost Town&quot; be also a plausible explanation for Lupus Wealth? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would imagine though that wealthy though he may be, this Lupus is NOT going to be popular with the local &quot;Bird and Lizard Population.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Naaah.<br /> <br /> &quot;I opened a caern of plenty, after much negotiation with the sept leader&quot; <br /> <br /> will that work for a start.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing on bone gnawers with Resources, is it beond the realm of reason for a Glasswalker, or Fang to &quot;Reward&quot; a Gnawer that completes a sufficiently important mission with a wad of Hundreds, but to do so with a &quot;Here doggy&quot; attitude?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T23:57:19-08:00","id":1027475,"title":"","content":"It's not the beyond the realm of reason to happen, but said Glass Walker or Silver Fang is going to regret it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T05:20:08-08:00","id":1027549,"title":"","content":"It is more likely that a rich Silver Fang will pay them for their services. A Resources 5 character is probably worth a minimum $500,000,000 and will probably have a minimum income of $50,000,000 from investments and properties (wealthier people get much better investment opportunities than poorer people). They will probably have a minimum of $15,000,000 of discretionary income per year, allowing them to give a lot of people Resources 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T05:31:09-08:00","id":1027554,"title":"","content":"Lot of people have misconceptions about Lupus Garou, confusing them with regular wolves. Don't do that &amp; lot of hings becomes clearer.<br /> <br /> A Rank 1 werewolf has already integrated into a tribal society &amp; usually became a member of a Caern.<br /> In modern times the Caers are situated at least in urban periphery, so being unaccustumated to the humanity can become a serious breach of the Veil.<br /> <br /> No sane Caern would accept this risk &amp; would designate homids to teach their lupus kin. (The Red Talons are an exeption.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:45:01-08:00","id":1027599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1027554#post1027554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No sane Caern would accept this risk &amp; would designate homids to teach their lupus kin. (The Red Talons are an exeption.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there is a bit of back and forth. Homid Garou teach Lupus Garou how to buy food in a store. Lupus Garou teach Homid Garou how to hunt food in the forest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:15:37-08:00","id":1027795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1027475#post1027475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the beyond the realm of reason to happen, but said Glass Walker or Silver Fang is going to regret it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> how so if I may ask? <br /> <br /> I like to play asshole Silver fangs I'll admit<br /> <br /> oh at the grand Masquerade, My first LARP Experience ever I wondered, would my silver fang galliard get glory or honor, for using himself as a decoy to distract bsds saving his pack in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T16:16:48-08:00","id":1027902,"title":"","content":"Um, because the Rabble basically exists to make life hell for asshole Garou that think they can piss on the Gnawers with impunity? The Gnawers turn their low class invisibility into a weapon to ferret out every last dirty secret, create every complication they can muster, and so on. Everything that asshole does is going to find itself sabotaged at every level, while their rivals seem to constantly get the leg up. Because the Gnawers hear things, see things, and go places that ensure their efforts are felt even if you never ever can prove it was them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T17:42:39-08:00","id":1027943,"title":"","content":"Having seen an (2 year old) &quot;Animal Planet&quot; documentary on *Urban* Wolves that prowl the cities of Illinois by night, with a per-City average of two-<b>thousand</b>, it would be safe to assume Chicago would have a rather healthily-sized Lupus Bone Gnawer (and Garou in general) population<br /> <br /> On that note:<br /> <br /> 1) Don Al Capone was one of the first racial-egalitarians of the 20th century, being one of the first White Employers in 20th century America with a multicultural Employee makeup (Asian, Black, Hispanic AND White); a Robin Hood who gave the oppressed/downtrodden social outcasts a place to go.<br /> Surely Chicago Bone Gnawers would have followed suit and created similarly philanthropic multicultural criminal sindicate?<br /> <br /> And I have a feeling Don Capone would be regarded as a Hero amongst the Bone Gnawers for the above reasons too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> 2) since the urban Wolf population is healthier than expected, linking to the above point; would seeking employment with the Dailo/Oyabun/Don/Boss of the local neigbourhoods's Triad/Yakuza/Mafia/Gang be a good starting point to justify Lupus resources? And if yes, which tribe have would have the best Crime Boss for a Lupus? Bone Gnawer/Glass Walker/Fianna/Shadow Lord?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-06-2017, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T19:53:48-08:00","id":1027992,"title":"","content":"Hm, the 'Urban Wolf' is actually a highly successful mixture of coyote, dog, and wolf (<a href=\"http://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/a-new-wolf-coyote-hybrid-is-infiltrating-our-cities\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.atlasobscura.com/articles...ing-our-cities</a>). I doubt that it would be considered non-domesticated enough to be breeding stock for Garou or Nuwisha, though I do agree that Bone Gnawer Wolf Kinfolk may be scruffy enough to be confused for an 'Urban Wolf'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T08:39:42-08:00","id":1028167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1027992#post1027992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, the 'Urban Wolf' is actually a highly successful mixture of coyote, dog, and wolf (<a href=\"http://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/a-new-wolf-coyote-hybrid-is-infiltrating-our-cities\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.atlasobscura.com/articles...ing-our-cities</a>). I doubt that it would be considered non-domesticated enough to be breeding stock for Garou or Nuwisha, though I do agree that Bone Gnawer Wolf Kinfolk may be scruffy enough to be confused for an 'Urban Wolf'.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd probably headcanon that in the World of Darkness, Urban Wolves are just Bone Gnawer Wolf kin.<br /> <br /> Now, the Bone Gnawers may have issues with their Lupus kin breeding with dogs. That may be an interesting plot point for a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T09:48:32-08:00","id":1028191,"title":"","content":"Yes, and with coyotes. What is the definition of a pure enough wolf to be Wolf Kinfolk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T12:57:35-08:00","id":1028243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1028191#post1028191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and with coyotes. What is the definition of a pure enough wolf to be Wolf Kinfolk?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also probably going to end up as a very uncomfortable conversation with the nuwisha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:36:40-08:00","id":1028274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1026232-lupus-with-resources-how-the-heck-does-that-make-sense?p=1027992#post1027992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, the 'Urban Wolf' is actually a highly successful mixture of coyote, dog, and wolf (<a href=\"http://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/a-new-wolf-coyote-hybrid-is-infiltrating-our-cities\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.atlasobscura.com/articles...ing-our-cities</a>). I doubt that it would be considered non-domesticated enough to be breeding stock for Garou or Nuwisha, though I do agree that Bone Gnawer Wolf Kinfolk may be scruffy enough to be confused for an 'Urban Wolf'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The article says those things are ~88% coyote DNA. Good for 'camouflage' in cities but nowhere near enough Gaian wolfblood to be useful kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 01-07-2017, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T00:32:50-08:00","id":1028455,"title":"","content":"Depending which edition we're using, crossbreeding with Nuwisha kin wouldn't be a big deal for the Gnawers (since Purebreed is already out of the picture). While IIRC the material that covered this was discussing human kin mating across Fera lines, there's no reason it wouldn't apply to coyote and wolf kin as they're breeding compatible (something none of the others have to worry about).<br /> <br /> Though this sort of thing is one of the reasons I want to retcon the setting to eliminate the Nuwisha as a separate Changing Breed (I'd make them an inter-Tribal Camp that started between the Pure Ones and has expanded a bit since) and expand the Garou to cover more species. If lynx and lion can both be Bastet despite no natural way to hybridize, then coyotes and wolves can be the same Changing Breed since they regularly do hybridize in the wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}